# What the repository leaves out. Everything the studio, the API, the tests and the deploy package read is committed;
# see RESTORE.md for what stays on the development Mac and why. Patterns are anchored (leading /) so that a folder
# name such as references/ or models/ is only excluded where meant.

# ---- environments, dependencies, build outputs, caches (recreated by uv sync / pnpm install / vite build)
.venv/
node_modules/
dist/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.swarm/
.claude-flow/
/agentdb.rvf
/agentdb.rvf.lock
/ruvector.db
.DS_Store
._*
# iCloud conflict copies ("name 2.json", "dist 3")
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]/

# ---- user state, databases and machine-specific locks (the API recreates them)
/data/*.sqlite*
/data/generated/
/data/imported-models/.canonical-v2-deploy.lock

# ---- licences and private links that must not travel
/disease-releases/clinical-nc-v3/
/artifacts/disease/clinical-nc-run-v1/
/docs/FINAL_DELIVERY_LINKS.md

# ---- training outputs, deliveries, evidence and benchmarks: on the Mac, not here (RESTORE.md lists them)
